      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Mundilferi is said to have fathered the moon and the flaming sun, whose courses mark time for humans.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Delling is named as the father of day, Nor as the begetter of night, and the gods are said to have fashioned the full and waning moon.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Vindsval is named as winter's father and Svosuth as the begetter of summer.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Bergelmir is described as born before the earth was made, as the son of Thruthgelmir and grandson of Aurgelmir.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Venom is said to have dropped down from Elivagar, grown until it became a giant, and given rise to the race of giants.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Under the arms of an unnamed ice giant, a male child and a female child grew together; a six-headed son was fashioned through contact of the feet.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Bergelmir is said to have been borne in an old boat.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Hrsvelg sits at the end of heaven in the guise of an eagle, and wind comes from his wings.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "Njorth was created in the home of the Wanes, given to the gods as a pledge, and is said to return to the Wanes when the world falls.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:12",
      "text": "The heroes in Othin's hall go out to fight each day, fall against one another, and soon become fully healed before sitting again.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:13",
      "text": "Vafthruthnir claims knowledge of the runes of the gods and giants, says he has reached every world, and names Niflhel beneath as the home where dead men dwell.",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:14",
      "text": "During the mighty winter, Lif and Lifthrasir are said to hide in Hoddmimir's wood and live on morning dews.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:9"
      ]
    },
