      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Rdbeh hears Mihrb's praise, becomes attracted to Zal, and privately confesses her love to her attendants.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5",
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Rdbeh's attendants object to her attachment by citing her reputation, Zal's white hair, his being raised by a Mountain Bird, and his uncertain human parentage.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Rdbeh maintains that her choice is fixed and rejects alternative royal or wealthy suitors named in her declaration.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "After recognizing that Rdbeh will not change her mind, the attendants agree to help bring Zal and Rdbeh together.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "In spring, Rdbeh's attendants go near Zal's halting-place and pretend to gather roses along the banks of a clear stream.",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "Zal sees the attendants, follows the river, and shoots a bird rising from the water; his servant retrieves the bird.",
