  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "Lohursp's administration is described as highly just and paternal, and he says that he intends to be especially moderate and clem ent toward the poor.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Lohursp is said to have four sons: Ardshr and Shydasp by the daughter of Kai-ks, and Gushtsp and Zarr by another woman.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Gushtsp is described as intrepid and acute, apparently suited for sovereignty, but not favored by his father because of his independent conduct.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Gushtsp gathers one hundred thousand horsemen and travels toward Hindustan without his father's authorization; Lohursp sends Zarr with one thousand horsemen to persuade him to return.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Gushtsp says that he and Zarr lack Kainian blood, cannot expect the diadem or throne from Lohursp, and must seek another way to advance their fortunes.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Zarr persuades Gushtsp to return on the condition that Gushtsp be named heir and treated with appropriate respect; Lohursp does not favor him, and Gushtsp then leaves his father's house for Rm.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "In Rm, Gushtsp lives in solitude and seeks work as a scribe, with a master of camel-drivers, and in a blacksmith's shop because he is hungry and poor.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "The first blow Gushtsp strikes with a blacksmith's hammer breaks the anvil, and the angry blacksmith expels him.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "A husbandman finds Gushtsp sitting in sorrow and tears, asks about his grief, takes him home, and gives him food.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Gushtsp and the husbandman identify themselves as descendants of Hsheng and Feridun respectively and conclude that they share an origin; they live together as friends for a considerable time.",
