      "text": "Gushtsp crowns Isfendiyr as his successor and instructs him to conquer other countries rather than remain in peace and private gratification.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Zerdusht recommends that Isfendiyr subdue kingdoms in order to diffuse the new religion, and Isfendiyr establishes the religion of the fire-worshippers in Rm, Hindstn, Arabia, and other countries.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "The sovereign of Rm adopts the faith of Zerdusht and accepts the Zendavesta as a spiritual instructor after being unable to resist Isfendiyr's incursions.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Gurzam, a warrior favored by Gushtsp but secretly hostile to Isfendiyr, tells the king that Isfendiyr intends to rebel and make him a prisoner.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Gushtsp reacts with great vexation, drinks wine for three days without sleep or rest, and then sends a letter summoning Isfendiyr.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Isfendiyr dreams that his father is angry with him; Jamsp confirms the anger and advises him to obey his father because Gushtsp is both king and father.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Isfendiyr appoints his eldest son Bahman to command the army during his absence and takes his other three sons, Mihrbs, Avir, and Nshhder, with him.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Gushtsp prepares measures to secure Isfendiyr as a prisoner, accuses him of usurping authority, and rejects Isfendiyr's declaration that he remains his father's servant and will resign his honors at the king's pleasure.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Isfendiyr is ordered into the tower-prison of a fort on an adjacent mountain and is bound with chains to four iron columns.",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
