      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "A Voice inside a Tavern asks why a drowsy Worshipper remains outside while the Temple is prepared.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "People before the Tavern call for the Door to be opened because they will stay only briefly and may not return after departing.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "The New Year revives old desires; a thoughtful Soul withdraws into solitude, where the White Hand of Moses appears on a Bough and Jesus is said to breathe from the Ground.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Iram is gone, Jemshd's seven-ringed Cup is lost, but a Ruby remains in the Vine and gardens grow beside Water.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "The Nightingale calls for red wine to make the Rose's cheek red.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "The speaker urges filling the Cup and casting off a Winter garment of Repentance in the fire of Spring; the Bird of Time has little distance left to fly.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "The Wine of Life oozes drop by drop and the Leaves of Life fall one by one; new roses appear while the Rose of yesterday is gone.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3",
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "The speaker and a beloved are placed beside Herbage between desert and cultivated land, where social distinctions are forgotten and a book, wine, bread, and singing accompany them.",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "The speaker describes the Worldly Hope as turning to ashes or disappearing like snow on a desert, and compares the world to a Caravanserai whose inhabitants stay for a destined hour and leave.",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "A Lion and a Lizard occupy the courts where Jemshd once gloried, while a Wild Ass stamps over the head of the sleeping Bahrm.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:12",
      "text": "The speaker imagines roses, hyacinths, and river-bank herb as connected with the blood, heads, or lips of formerly beautiful people.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:13",
      "text": "People loved by the speaker have drunk their Cup before him and gone to rest; those now celebrating must descend beneath the earth and lie in dust without wine, song, or singer.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:14",
      "text": "A Muezzin from a Tower of Darkness declares that the reward of those focused on today or tomorrow is neither here nor there.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:15",
      "text": "Saints and Sages are described as scattered like foolish prophets, with their words mocked and their mouths stopped with dust.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:16",
      "text": "The young speaker visits a Doctor and Saint, hears arguments, and leaves through the same door by which he entered.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:17",
      "text": "The speaker says that he came like Water and goes like Wind, without knowing why or from where he entered or where he will go.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:18",
      "text": "The speaker rises from Earth's Centre through the Seventh Gate, sits on Saturn's Throne, and unravels many knots but not the master-knot of human fate.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:19",
      "text": "The speaker finds a Door without a Key and a Veil that cannot be seen through; after some talk of the speaker and the beloved, there is no more of either.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:20",
      "text": "Earth, the Seas, and rolling Heaven do not answer the speaker's questions about existence and fate.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
